      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Practice -ar",
        "body": "Today we walk through this idea step by step. To conjugate means to change the verb for the person (I, you, he/she). The stem is what remains after you drop -ar. The ending is the new tip (present: I -o, you -as, he/she -a).\n\nLet's keep going together. example cantar: drop -ar → cant- (stem). cant- + -o = canto; + -as = cantas; + -a = canta.\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Conjugate cantar and hablar for I/you/he. Underline the stem and circle the ending. Write three short sentences.\n\nError común: Before we finish, one warning. Writing yo cantar. Correct: yo canto (stem cant- + ending -o)."
      }
    ],
    "summary": ""
  },
